## Entity business rules (SWRL) in Studio, Explorer and MCP

Context: Ontology designers can attach SWRL business rules to a class in
Studio. Builders then run a rule on one entity from the Graph Explorer
(confirmation modal) or through a new MCP tool (no confirmation). The rule
runs scoped to that entity, the inferred triples are materialised into the
graph, and the Explorer canvas refreshes. Candidate rules are those whose
atoms cite the class or one of its parent classes. The Cypher translator
(Neo4j) is still scaffolding, so Neo4j domains infer no facts.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyRules.py
   Rule/class matching (swrl_rule_classes, rules_for_class with lineage),
   focus variables, and rename/drop cascade of class business_rules refs.
2. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyClassModel.py,
   src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py, src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py
   Persist the class business_rules list (ontobricks:businessRules JSON literal).
3. src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLSQLTranslator.py, SWRLEngine.py, ReasoningService.py
   Optional entity focus filter on the inference SQL, threaded through run_swrl_rules.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/NodeBusinessRuleService.py (new), NodeContextService.py, __init__.py
   Policy-gated class entries, allow-list resolution, entity-scoped run and
   materialisation, business_rules in node context.
5. src/back/core/mcp_tools.py
   New domain tool run_entity_business_rule and context feature business_rules.
6. src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py, src/api/routers/internal/_graph_access.py
   POST /api/v1/digitaltwin/nodes/business-rule with Builder write gate
   (assert_public_graph_write); business_rules in node context response.
7. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Confirm-gated /dtwin/nodes/business-rule/request|confirm|cancel (Builder);
   token kind isolation from actions; business_rules in /dtwin/classes.
8. src/api/routers/domains.py, src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   business_rules in domain classes; SWRL save/delete cascades class refs.
9. src/mcp-server/server/constants.py, tools.py, formatting.py
   run_entity_business_rule tool, business rules in describe_ontology,
   class context and node context output.
10. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js, ontology-swrl.js,
    ontology-information.js, src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
    Studio References "Business rules" block, selector modal, front cascade.
11. src/front/static/query/js/query-business-rules.js (new), query-loaders.js,
    query-sigmagraph.js, query-entity-details.js, src/front/templates/dtwin.html
    Explorer details section, context-menu entries, confirmation modal,
    result table and graph refresh.
12. docs/api.md, docs/mcp.md, docs/data-access.md, docs/user-guide.md, docs/features.md
    Document the endpoint, tool, policy element, Builder requirement and Neo4j limitation.
13. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-05-entity-business-rules-design.md (new)
    Design spec.
14. tests/units/dtwin/test_entity_business_rules.py, tests/units/api/test_dtwin_nodes_business_rule.py,
    tests/units/mcp/test_business_rule_tool.py, tests/units/front/test_entity_business_rules_ui.py (new);
    tests/units/core/test_mcp_tools_policy.py, tests/units/mcp/test_domain_policy_gating.py
    New coverage; tool counts updated.

